/-!
# Critical prime translation defeats every symmetric rank-two boundary correction

The actual compact theta divisor vector is promoted to the cross-polarized quantile root-mode
interface.  A divisor copy and its critical-line reflection then have zero mixed pinned-boundary
pairing, while their diagonal pinned-boundary currents are exact negatives.  Consequently the
whole reflection-symmetric Hermitian correction generated by the rank-two pinned Green form is
identically blind on the pair.

This closes the first non-diagonal repair suggested by the critical-rigging no-go.  Even after an
arbitrary symmetric rank-two boundary correction, the reflected pair's centered prime-translation
energy retains the strict `cosh` excess.  A surviving Route-P Ward producer must therefore leave
the local rank-two pinned-moment algebra: it must be source-nonlocal or break reflection symmetry
before its final positive reduction.
-/

open Complex Real MeasureTheory Set Filter Topology
